1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
That pop from your exhaust

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,000
when you let off the gas isn't just loud.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
A bang or backfire on deceleration —

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
not every time, but enough to notice.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
One clue: unburned fuel igniting late,

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
in the exhaust instead of the cylinder.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
That can point to a vacuum leak,

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
a misfire, or a mixture running rich.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Don't guess which one.

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
A scan and a listen can narrow it down fast.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before a pop becomes a bigger repair.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
